.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ECCE-QM, B3LYP/6-31G*, relaxed scan of the H-C-C-H torsion, -180 to 180 degrees in 25 points. This calculation shows the internal rotation of ethane: in the Relaxed Scan panel the energy is lowest, 0.0 kJ/mol, for the staggered geometries at -180, -60, 60 and 180 degrees and highest, 11.8 kJ/mol, for the eclipsed ones at -120, 0 and 120 degrees, so the rotation barrier is 11.8 kJ/mol (electronic energies, no zero-point correction).
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ECCE-QM
